= Template System Validation Framework: Ensuring SMW Integration Integrity =

== Executive Summary

BITwiki's template system serves as the interface between human-readable content and machine-queryable knowledge graphs. This framework establishes validation criteria ensuring templates enhance rather than hinder recursive knowledge development.

'''Core Principle:''' Templates must be '''epistemically transparent''' and '''semantically queryable'''—every template invocation should contribute to the knowledge graph, not obscure it.

----
== 1. Validation Dimensions

=== 1.1 Semantic Integrity

Templates must correctly set and retrieve SMW properties:

| Validation Check | Pass Criteria | Failure Mode |
|------------------|---------------|--------------|
| Property Setting | `[[Has property::value]]` renders correctly | Silent property failure |
| Property Retrieval | `{{#show:Page|?Has property}}` returns value | Empty or wrong value |
| Type Consistency | Values match [[Has type::...]] declaration | Type mismatch errors |
| Multi-Value Support | `[[Has property::val1]],[[Has property::val2]]` works | Only last value stored |

'''Test Pattern:'''
```mediawiki
{{#vardefine: test_value | {{#show: TestPage | ?Has test property }} }}
{{#if: {{#var: test_value}} | PASS | FAIL }}
```

=== 1.2 Epistemic Transparency

Templates must expose epistemic status, not hide it:

| Validation Check | Pass Criteria | Failure Mode |
|------------------|---------------|--------------|
| Epistemic Marker | `{{EpistemicIcon|Established}}` displays | Icon missing |
| Confidence Display | Confidence value visible to readers | Hidden in template |
| Status Editable | Users can modify epistemic fields | Hardcoded status |
| Provenance Chain | `[[Has author::...]]` traceable | Anonymous template output |

'''Critical Rule:''' No template should output content without epistemic marking.

=== 1.3 Transclusion Hygiene

Templates must respect inclusion boundaries:

| Validation Check | Pass Criteria | Failure Mode |
|------------------|---------------|--------------|
| Noinclude Tags | `{{Documentation}}` present | Documentation leaks |
| Includeonly Content | Only intended content transcludes | Template code visible |
| Category Isolation | Categories in `` blocks | Category pollution |
| Parameter Sanitization | `{{{param|default}}}` has defaults | Broken transclusions |

'''Validation Query:'''
```bash
grep -L "<noinclude>" *.wiki  # Find templates missing noinclude
grep "\\[\\[Category:" *.wiki | grep -v "noinclude"  # Find category leaks
```

=== 1.4 Recursive Compatibility

Templates must support recursive knowledge patterns:

| Validation Check | Pass Criteria | Failure Mode |
|------------------|---------------|--------------|
| Self-Reference | Template can reference its own output | Infinite recursion |
| Query Integration | `{{#ask:...}}` works inside template | Parser function conflicts |
| Nested Templates | `{{TemplateA|{{TemplateB}}}}` resolves | Nested failure |
| Dynamic Properties | `[[Has {{#var:prop}}::value]]` works | Property name literal |

----
== 2. Template Categories

=== 2.1 Infobox Templates

'''Purpose:''' Structured entity representation

'''Validation Criteria:'''
* All parameters map to SMW properties
* Epistemic status field mandatory
* Image handling with fallback
* Mobile-responsive CSS

'''Example: Infobox_Concept'''
```mediawiki
<includeonly>{{#if: {{{title|}}}
| {{#set:
  |Has entity type=Concept
  |Has title={{{title}}}
  |Has epistemic status={{{epistemic_status|Hypothetical}}}
  |Has confidence={{{confidence|0.5}}}
  |Has domain={{{domain|}}}
  }}
<div class="infobox concept">
  <div class="infobox-header">
    <span class="epistemic-marker">{{EpistemicIcon|{{{epistemic_status|Hypothetical}}}}}</span>
    <span class="infobox-title">{{{title}}}</span>
    <span class="confidence-badge">{{ConfidenceBar|{{{confidence|0.5}}}}}</span>
  </div>
  ...
</div>
| {{Error|Infobox_Concept requires title parameter}}
}}</includeonly>
<noinclude>{{Documentation}}[[Category:Infobox Templates]]
```

'''Validation Checklist:'''
* [ ] All parameters have `{{#set:...}}` mappings
* [ ] Epistemic status defaults to "Hypothetical"
* [ ] Confidence defaults to 0.5
* [ ] Error handling for missing required params
* [ ] Documentation in ``

=== 2.2 Epistemic Marker Templates

'''Purpose:''' Visual and semantic epistemic classification

'''Validation Criteria:'''
* Icon displays correctly
* Tooltip explains status
* Screen reader accessible
* Links to epistemic framework

'''Example: EpistemicIcon'''
```mediawiki
<includeonly>{{#switch: {{{1|Hypothetical}}}
| Axiomatic = <span class="epistemic axiomatic" title="Axiomatic: Self-evident or definitional (confidence 1.0)">⚡</span>
| Established = <span class="epistemic established" title="Established: Well-supported by evidence (confidence 0.8-0.99)">✓</span>
| Emerging = <span class="epistemic emerging" title="Emerging: Preliminary evidence exists (confidence 0.5-0.79)">~</span>
| Hypothetical = <span class="epistemic hypothetical" title="Hypothetical: Speculative, needs testing (confidence 0.0-0.49)">?</span>
| Contested = <span class="epistemic contested" title="Contested: Active disagreement (confidence varies)">!</span>
| #default = <span class="epistemic unknown" title="Unknown: Status not specified">◌</span>
}}</includeonly>
```

'''Validation Tests:'''
* `{{EpistemicIcon|Established}}` → displays ✓
* `{{EpistemicIcon}}` → defaults to ?
* `{{EpistemicIcon|Invalid}}` → displays ◌

=== 2.3 Query Templates

'''Purpose:''' Reusable semantic queries

'''Validation Criteria:'''
* Query returns expected results
* Empty result handling
* Performance optimization (LIMIT, sort)
* Parameterized queries

'''Example: RelatedEntities'''
```mediawiki
<includeonly>{{#ask: [[Has related entity::{{FULLPAGENAME}}]]
|?Has title
|?Has epistemic status
|?Has confidence
|format=table
|limit={{{limit|10}}}
|sort=Has confidence
|order=desc
|intro=<div class="related-entities">
|outro=</div>
|default=<div class="no-related">No related entities found.</div>
}}</includeonly>
```

'''Validation Tests:'''
* Query executes without timeout
* Results sorted by confidence
* Empty result shows default message
* Limit parameter respected

=== 2.4 Navigation Templates

'''Purpose:''' Cross-page knowledge navigation

'''Validation Criteria:'''
* All links valid
* Dynamic generation via queries
* Current page highlighting
* Epistemic status indicators on links

