== 5. Template Deprecation Protocol

=== 5.1 Deprecation Criteria

Templates should be deprecated when:
* Functionality moved to other systems (e.g., BITHUB for agent templates)
* Superseded by better implementations
* Security vulnerabilities discovered
* Performance issues unresolvable

=== 5.2 Deprecation Process

# '''Mark Deprecated:''' Add `{{Deprecated}}` template
# '''Document Migration:''' Provide replacement instructions
# '''Update References:''' Replace usages in existing pages
# '''Archive:''' Move to `Category:Deprecated Templates`
# '''Remove:''' After deprecation period (6 months)

'''Example Deprecation:'''
```mediawiki
<noinclude>{{Deprecated|reason=Agent documentation moved to BITHUB|replacement=BITHUB:Agent_Documentation}}
<includeonly>{{Error|This template is deprecated. Use [[BITHUB:Agent_Documentation]] instead.}}</includeonly>
```

----
== 6. Performance Optimization

=== 6.1 Query Optimization

| Anti-Pattern | Optimization |
|--------------|--------------|
| Unbounded `{{#ask:...}}` | Add `|limit=50` |
| Deep nesting | Flatten template calls |
| Repeated queries | Use `{{#vardefine:...}}` |
| Complex filters | Pre-compute with concepts |

=== 6.2 Caching Strategy
* Use `|cache=...` for expensive queries
* Mark volatile content with `|no cache`
* Leverage SMW's built-in query cache

----
== 7. Conclusion

Template validation ensures BITwiki's knowledge infrastructure remains:
* '''Semantically queryable:''' Every template contributes to the knowledge graph
* '''Epistemically transparent:''' Confidence and status are always visible
* '''Recursively compatible:''' Templates compose without breaking
* '''Maintainable:''' Clear validation criteria enable systematic review

'''Recommendation:''' Implement automated validation pipeline using the checks in Section 3.1. Require manual review for all new templates using Section 3.2 checklist.

